      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Alternatively they could have looked at existing VR screenshot systems and known that they give you a 5 second countdown before the screenshot is taken. I think steamvr might be the only system that does not because it can be taken with controller inputs avoiding your described issue. I know that Oculus and WMR both give you timers because they are activated from a menu.\nTechnically they could also do something custom like waiting until you press the trigger on your controller after activating the screenshot, etc. Either way if its activated from a menu you need to give time to get things in or out of frame. Unless they are actively trying to discourage the use of screenshots, even though you can already do such things on multiple VR headsets from their overlays.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
