      "value": "@{5bb80f6b2297f24ce1ccb151|full_name}: Thinking about the two methods I’d say if they want the instantaneous screenshot your method can achieve that as it allows pure controller inputs, like the steamvr screenshots. If they have it as a button anywhere that requires you to look at it, then a timer can assist with letting the menu item close and having the user frame what is needed, like oculus and wmr.\nTwo methods, both would work to solve the awkward button they have at the moment.\nSomething to consider with the current ui and the new one is the ability to take a screenshot of something in the menu with their own screenshot tool. The timer also usually means the user needs to manually close the menu if they don’t want that in the screenshot. If the action menu worked Independently of the main menu then a timer there can allow screenshots to include any of the menus.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-18T12:47:08.220Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While it's great that a screenshot button was added to the quick menu, it's a little awkward to use in VR because you need to be looking at the menu to click the button and use both of your hands, which often results is your hands being in the screenshot.\nI think screenshots are much better at capturing moments than a camera sometimes, as people don't try to pose and act natural. \nHaving the ability to take one from the action menu would mean you don't have to look at the menu anymore to be able to click it, making it a lot easier to use.",
